  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Trail Blaze on Granite",
    "overview": "Feedcut is a trail sign, not a dashboard. Its one job on screen is to say whether the gate holds, and it says it the way a mountain trail does: a white-red-white blaze painted on stone. Whole paint means Feedcut is cutting the feeds; the same three bands drawn but unpainted mean it is off; a blaze snapped in two and knocked out of line, painted trail yellow, means Android stopped it. A sentence under the blaze always says the same thing in words.\n\nThe ground is stone: granite (#17191A) in dark mode, a pale limestone in light mode, both first-class. Signage is set in Barlow Condensed, the narrow bold face of painted trail boards, and everything people read as sentences stays in the system sans. The screen is a single ruled column: hairline-separated rows, no cards, no elevation, generous gaps between sections. The day's count is the one oversized element, cut in 112sp condensed numerals, and the last seven days sit on a fixed scale so a bar's length is its minutes. The world refuses the category default of a purple Material card with a big number.\n\nDensity is low and the tone is strict. The screen is opened rarely and glanced at, so status, count and history are visible without scrolling once setup is done; setup itself appears as a short trail of waymarks only until it is finished.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One painted blaze carries the status: ON (whole), OFF (unpainted outline), STUCK (snapped, trail yellow).",
      "Paint is scarce: blaze red and white appear where Feedcut works or where the next step is, nowhere else.",
      "Barlow Condensed for signage, system sans for reading.",
      "Flat granite or limestone ground, 1dp hairlines instead of cards, no shadows.",
      "Cut-board corners (3dp, 2dp at waymark size); no pills on owned components.",
      "History on a fixed 120-minute scale, past days in moss, today in red."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Scarce Paint Rule",
        "body": "Blaze red and blaze white mark only what is working or what to do next: the ON blaze, a done waymark, the one filled button, a checked switch, today's bar. No red headings, red icons or red decoration.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Yellow Means Check Rule",
        "body": "Trail yellow and ochre appear only when something needs checking: the STUCK blaze and a \"rule may be broken\" detail line. Never as an accent.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Moss Is History Rule",
        "body": "Past days are moss; only today is red. Moss is not used for success, status or buttons.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Signage and Reading Rule",
        "body": "Barlow Condensed is for signs: the wordmark, status, count, section headings, buttons and week figures. Anything read as a sentence (details, instructions, notes) is in the system sans. Uppercase is used only for the wordmark, section headings and button labels.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Honest Number Rule",
        "body": "Estimates are marked in the type itself: \"≈\" leads the minutes, and the estimate note sits directly under it in body small.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Fixed Scale Rule",
        "body": "In the week view, 120 minutes is the full bar width on every day, in every week. Longer days are drawn full and labelled \"N min+\". Never scale bars to the week's maximum.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hairline Not Card Rule",
        "body": "Group with 1dp hairlines and space. Content sits directly on the ground.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Painted Not Lifted Rule",
        "body": "Things are painted on the stone, never floated above it. State changes change paint, never elevation.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Cut Board Rule",
        "body": "Feedcut's own shapes (buttons, blaze, waymarks, icon boards) have 2 to 3dp corners. No pills, no circles, no large radii on anything the app draws; platform switches are the exception.",
        "section": "shapes"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do pair every colored state with words: the status sentence under the blaze, the detail line on an app row.",
      "Do keep exactly one filled button on a screen, for the next step; make the rest outlined.",
      "Do keep the week view on its fixed 120-minute scale and mark overflow with \"min+\".",
      "Do set signage in Barlow Condensed and sentences in the system sans.",
      "Do separate rows with 1dp hairlines and sections with space (20, 28 or 36dp).",
      "Do use 3dp corners on buttons and blaze shapes, 2dp on waymark-sized marks.",
      "Do design light and dark together from the same materials: limestone and granite grounds, deep blaze red and blaze red primaries.",
      "Do lead any estimated number with \"≈\" and keep its assumption visible next to it."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't put content in cards, add shadows or raise elevation on the main screens.",
      "Don't use blaze red for decoration, headings or icons.",
      "Don't use trail yellow or ochre for anything that is not a \"check this\" state.",
      "Don't use pill or circular shapes on Feedcut's own buttons, marks or icon; platform switches are the only round control.",
      "Don't auto-scale the week bars to the largest day.",
      "Don't use purple or default Material tonal palettes; colors come from the stone, the blaze paints, moss and trail yellow.",
      "Don't show the setup trail once setup is done."
    ]
  }
}
